diagnosis
  every upstream this job type depends on (api.globalping.io, rdap.org,
  ip-api.com, ipwho.is, dns.google) is outside this execution
  environment's outbound network allowlist. The proxy's own status
  endpoint (http://127.0.0.1:35841/__agentproxy/status) confirms the
  rejections as "connect_rejected ... policy denial", and the ip-api.com
  attempt (routed as plain HTTP rather than a CONNECT tunnel) returns the
  allowlist's own message verbatim: "Host not in allowlist: ip-api.com.
  Add this host to your network egress settings to allow access."
  This is a static per-environment configuration, not a transient
  outage — a same-attempt retry against any of the five hosts reproduced
  the identical rejection, so a second or third job attempt in this same
  environment would fail identically. No probe was created, so there is
  no measurementId and no probe/WHOIS/IP data to report on; fabricating
  any of §2-3 output would misrepresent this job's grounding in real
  Globalping data, so no probe-analysis.html or probe.json asset is
  produced for this attempt (see edge case §4 "API / network error").

decision
  attempt 1 recorded as failed, not retried automatically: the failure
  is an environment egress-allowlist restriction, not a Globalping-side
  or transient network condition, so an automatic re-attempt in this
  same environment cannot succeed. Unblocking requires the environment
  owner to add api.globalping.io, rdap.org, ip-api.com (or an HTTPS
  proxied/Pro base), ipwho.is and dns.google (or cloudflare-dns.com) to
  this environment's outbound network policy.

